  "context": "## Why AMBER and not RED\n\nThe computed colour was RED on the breach condition. A human override moved it to AMBER on the grounds that a workaround is in place. The override expires Jul 29 and is always shown with the computed colour beside it: \"the machine says red, the lead says amber, because Y\" is the useful sentence, and hiding either half breaks it.\n\n## The honest dynamic range\n\nOne RED condition has no live input at all — it needs a per-ask blocking marker no source carries, so it is structurally untestable rather than merely unmet this week. Naming that is the difference between a verdict that was checked and one that could not be.\n\n## Ask me about\n\nWhether the override should be renewed or allowed to lapse to the computed colour, and what it would take to give the dormant condition a real input."
